Our files are not that big at all, but some users tried whole-genome human data and they succeeded, ~24M CpGs, that would be ~24M rows. Our RRBS data has about ~4M CpGs. I think you should try read.table() and see if that works OK or not. That is important for me to know if it is a problem of R memory limits in general or methylKit.

Best,
Altuna

